## OpenAI browser OAuth sign-in correction — 2026-11-11

User-reported failure: after browser authentication, OpenAI displayed “This sign-in attempt has ended.”

Cause found in `internal/auth/openai.go`: Agy unconditionally appended the undocumented `prompt=consent` query parameter to every ChatGPT-plan authorization URL, including requests carrying a retained `id_token_hint`. This is the strongest code-level suspect; the provider-side error does not itself identify the rejected parameter.

Correction on `work`:
- Removed `prompt=consent`; authorization URL creation now lives in `buildOpenAIAuthorizeURL`.
- Preserved the documented initial-registration fields (`dynamic_agent_client`, `agent_name_hint`) and returning-registration fields (issued client ID, retained ID-token hint, optional email hint).
- Added regression tests for both authorization URL variants, including assertions that `prompt` is absent and the state, nonce, PKCE, scopes, resource, callback, and host ID remain intact.
- Official reference: OpenAI Sign in with ChatGPT “Registration and sign-in” documentation, checked 2026-11-11: https://developers.openai.com/siwc/token-sharing-open-source/sign-in

