## Provider and credential separation — implementation and verification — 2026-11-13

Implemented on branch `work`; core provider/credential commit: `353f8e3a46a3f5c32f7a0a30ba9072431fa120bd`.

### Provider routing

- Added explicit identities for Google Antigravity (`gemini`), Gemini Developer API (`gemini-api`), Google AI Studio (`ai-studio`), Gemini Live (`gemini-live`), ChatGPT OAuth (`openai`), OpenAI API (`openai-api`), local OpenAI-compatible (`openai-compatible`), and OpenRouter (`openrouter`).
- Provider selection applies the matching model default. Local OpenAI-compatible keeps an empty model until discovery rather than inheriting a cloud model.
- `agy models PROVIDER` resolves a separate provider client/catalogue and does not alter the active provider or configured model.
- Updated CLI aliases, Bash completions, descriptive TUI provider choices, and browser UI provider choices.
- The browser UI points users to the TUI/CLI for credentials and does not transmit API keys over the browser UI.

### Credential separation

- Added `internal/auth/apikey.go` with a provider-key store at `${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/agy-open/api-keys.json`.
- The fallback directory uses mode `0700`; the key file uses `0600`. Writes are temporary-file + sync + atomic rename. Status responses expose only source/provider/environment-variable names, never secret values.
- Environment variables are consulted only for the explicitly selected API-key provider. Provider-specific `AGY_*` keys precede shared aliases; saved keys are the fallback.
- Google Antigravity's `gemini.New` and ChatGPT's `openai.New` no longer read ambient public API-key variables.
- Added explicit-key constructors for Gemini Developer API, AI Studio, Gemini Live, OpenAI API, local OpenAI-compatible, and OpenRouter.
- Legacy OpenAI API keys are migrated from the old OpenAI OAuth file to the separate API-key store. ChatGPT OAuth authentication no longer treats an API key as an access token.
- The TUI exposes `/config → Provider credentials`: provider-specific status, masked key entry, save/update, model-catalogue validation, and saved-key removal. The prompt renderer masks secrets across full-screen and line modes and clears the input buffer after save/cancel.
- No OS keyring integration yet; the protected per-user file is the only storage backend.

### Model catalogues and transports

- Gemini Developer API has its own `/models` parser and keeps only models supporting `generateContent`.
- AI Studio uses its Interactions transport and provider-native catalogue. Gemini Live uses its direct WebSocket transport and Live-only catalogue.
- ChatGPT OAuth retains its account-specific catalogue. OpenAI API uses the public `/v1/models` response envelope and an explicit API key.
- Local OpenAI-compatible uses its configured endpoint and optional independent `AGY_LOCAL_API_KEY`.
- OpenRouter uses `https://openrouter.ai/api/v1`, requires its own key, adds `HTTP-Referer` and `X-Title`, and preserves returned model IDs.

### Regression coverage and CI

- Added tests for API-key store file/directory permissions, independent provider entries, key removal, status redaction, and environment-variable precedence.
- Added constructor tests proving Antigravity and ChatGPT OAuth ignore ambient API keys.
- Added explicit Gemini Developer API catalogue filtering and OpenAI API key request tests.
- Added TUI secret-input masking tests and provider display-name coverage.
- Added OpenRouter model-catalogue tests asserting selected-key bearer auth, identification headers, and model IDs.
- Added web UI assertions for all eight provider choices and the no-browser-secret-entry policy.
- Core provider isolation passed CI at `353f8e3a46a3f5c32f7a0a30ba9072431fa120bd` (run ID `43364706421`). After adding the eight-provider browser selector, descriptive TUI provider names, OpenRouter catalogue-request coverage, README/TODO/config-guide updates, and this verification record, the complete final implementation passed CI at `f2e55dec384b2f237d20a145b5a1db5f79a14d5e` (run ID `43366053056`). The final run passed Bash syntax/completion checks, installer tests, `gofmt`, `go test ./...`, `go vet ./...`, and static Linux/amd64 build.
- Three earlier CI failures were corrected before this passing run: stale constructor call/OpenAI API test setup, prompt-mask test expectation, and Gemini Live/OpenRouter environment precedence. The final run passed all steps.

### Remaining verification

- Do not claim live authentication based on environment presence or a successful model-list request. No user API keys were read, logged, or used for live provider calls in this implementation pass.
- Still required: run a real text-generation request per API-key provider using credentials supplied by the user, and add an OS credential-store backend if desired.
